---
import StatusBadge from "../ui/StatusBadge.astro";

/** Shown when the demo gate is not configured in this build. Nothing here is a live read. */
interface Props {
  missing: readonly string[];
  invalid: string | null;
}

const { missing, invalid } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="app-unavailable" aria-labelledby="unavailable-title">
  <StatusBadge tone="awaiting">Not live</StatusBadge>
  <h2 id="unavailable-title">Demo gate not deployed yet</h2>
  <p>
    This page runs live attacks against a separate demo gate on NEAR testnet. That gate is not part
    of this build, so nothing here can run and nothing is shown as live.
  </p>
  <p>When it is deployed, this page will have:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A wallet connection and a one-time credit deposit, with a session key so runs do not nag.</li>
    <li>Several malicious upgrades, each refused by a different rule, repeatable without limit.</li>
    <li>The attested verifier's stages, live, and the recorded verdict with its rule and reason.</li>
    <li>The active rule set read from the gate, and a lookup for any proposal id.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Meanwhile the recorded runs of the final gate are on <a href="/#evidence">the home page</a>, and
    every claim can be checked from a terminal with <a href="/#try">the CLI commands</a> or <a href="/docs">the docs</a>.
  </p>
  <details>
    <summary>Build inputs</summary>
    {
      invalid !== null && <p>Present but refused: {invalid}.</p>
    }
    {
      missing.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <p>Missing:</p>
          <ul>
            {missing.map((name) => <li><code>{name}</code></li>)}
          </ul>
        </>
      )
    }
  </details>
</section>
